.TH GTASKS-OPEN 1 "2026-09-09" "gtasks-panel 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gtasks-open \- focus the Google Tasks app window, or open one
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gtasks-open
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gtasks-open
asks
.BR wmctrl (1)
to focus a window with class
.BR GoogleTasksApp .
If there is none, it starts Google Chrome, or Chromium as fallback, with
.B \-\-app=https://tasks.google.com
in its own profile directory.
.PP
A separate profile directory is necessary. A browser that already runs
with the default profile takes the URL and ignores the window class.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GTASKS_WIN_CLASS
Window class to look for and to set. Default
.BR GoogleTasksApp .
.TP
.B GTASKS_PROFILE_DIR
Browser profile directory. Default
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/google-chrome-tasks-app .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success. 1 when no Chrome or Chromium is found.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gtasks-panel (1),
.BR wmctrl (1)
